    {
      "turn": 1,
      "doctor_question": "Hello. I'm Dr. Smith. What brings you in to see me today?",
      "targeted_symptom": "S021",
      "patient_response": "Well, hello Dr. Smith. They, uh, they told me I needed to come in and talk to you because of how I've been talking lately. See, what brings me here is my talking gets all mixed up—or at least, that’s what everybody keeps telling me. I’ll be at work, you know, I clean the buildings over on the west side, mostly just doing the floors and the trash, and I try to explain things to the guys on the shift or the supervisor. \n\nLike, I try to explain about the keys, because you gotta understand how the master keys work with the different floors and the brass rings, but then that gets me talking about the jail. Because the locks are the same, you see? Heavy tumblers, the way they click. And the jail... well, that naturally brings up the prayer rug. I was trying to tell my supervisor the other night about the woven patterns on the prayer rug and how you have to face it, and then the chess pieces. The knights and the rooks, moving on the squares, just like the linoleum tiles I buff every single night. \n\nI try to lay it all out so they get the full picture of how it all connects, you know? The keys and the rug and the chess pieces, it all goes together if you just listen. But people just stop me and look at me like I'm crazy. They tell me they cannot follow what I am saying. They say I make no sense and I’m losing them and jumping all over the place. I don't mean to mix it all up, I'm just trying to give them the whole story so they understand, but my boss said I had to come see a doctor because they just can't understand my sentences anymore. So, I guess that's why I'm sitting here.",
