    {
      "turn": 3,
      "doctor_question": "Have you ever experienced periods lasting for several days or weeks where your mood was extremely high, or alternatively, periods where you felt so down or hopeless that you couldn't function?",
      "targeted_symptom": "S033",
      "patient_response": "Well, yeah, I have. I definitely have. See, sometimes—and this can go on for a couple of weeks, maybe more—I get this feeling like I am just on top of the world. I mean, I feel so high up, so powerful, like I've got electricity running right through my veins instead of blood. I'll be walking down the halls with my cart, and I just feel fantastic. I laugh, I talk real loud to everybody I see—the security guards, the delivery guys, even the folks working late in the offices. I just want to tell them all how great everything is, how I've got it all figured out, you know? \n\nI feel like I could clean the whole building in an hour and still have energy to run a marathon. But the thing is, Dr. Smith, it's a double-edged sword, because as good as I feel, if somebody crosses me during those times... watch out. If my supervisor comes up and asks why I haven't emptied the recycling on floor four yet, or if somebody questions how I'm doing my job, I just snap. It's like a switch flips. I get so irritable, so fast. I'll start shouting at them over the smallest little thing, just raising my voice right there in the hallway because how dare they question me when I'm feeling that powerful, right? \n\nI remember one time last month, I was having one of those really high weeks, feeling like a king pushing a mop, and the night manager just asked me to move my cart over a few inches so he could get by. Just a few inches! And I went off. I yelled so loud the echo went all the way down the corridor. I couldn't help it. So, yeah, I get those periods where I'm flying high and loud, but I can turn real mean and snappy if anybody gets in my way.",
