    {
      "turn": 4,
      "doctor_question": "When you have those weeks where you feel on top of the world or irritable, do the voices and the trouble with your talking happen at the same time, or do they ever happen when your mood is completely normal?",
      "targeted_symptom": "additional_requirement_3",
      "patient_response": "Well, that's the thing, Dr. Smith, that's exactly the thing. See, you'd think it would all just happen when I'm feeling like I've got lightning in my veins, or when I'm so low I can barely drag the mop bucket out of the closet. But it's not like that. Not at all. \n\nI remember, just a few months ago, maybe back in October when the leaves were turning and I had to sweep up all those wet, brown oak leaves from the front entrance every single night before I even started on the inside floors. I was feeling just fine. Regular, you know? Not flying high, not snapping at nobody, just coming in, punching my card at 10:00 PM, getting my coffee from the breakroom—black, no sugar, because the sugar makes the ants come out in the summer—and doing my job. My mood was completely normal. I wasn't too up, wasn't too down. Just calm.\n\nBut even then, even during those quiet weeks, and it lasted for a good two, maybe three weeks straight... I still heard him. I'd be polishing the brass on the elevator doors on the ground floor, feeling perfectly fine, and there he was. The man in the vents. Calling my name. Telling me I ruined it all. And it wasn't just the voice, Dr. Smith. During that same time, when I was feeling totally level, I started noticing the people in the building. The late-night accountants, the security guards on the graveyard shift. I knew they were signaling about me. \n\nI'd see them standing by the water cooler on the fourth floor, and one of them would tap his watch, or adjust his tie, or cough twice. And I knew, I just knew, they were sending messages about me. Coordinating. I tried to tell my supervisor about it, tried to explain how the double-cough connects to the way they leave their trash cans angled toward the door, but he just gave me that look again. But my mood was fine! I wasn't irritable at all. I was just trying to explain the signals. So yes, the voice and the... the connections, they happen even when I'm just feeling like my regular self, for weeks at a time. It doesn't ever really stop, even when my mood settles down.",
