      "turn": 5,
      "doctor_question": "Looking back over the past year or so, have there been any periods of at least two weeks where you experienced the voices or the feeling that people were signaling you, but you did NOT have any of those mood swings or changes in energy?",
      "targeted_symptom": "additional_requirement_3",
      "patient_response": "Well, yes, if I’m really looking back over the whole year... let me think on that. Yeah. Yeah, there definitely were. Like, take around late February, maybe early March. The snow was finally melting outside, which makes a huge, muddy mess in the main lobby, let me tell you. People track in all that slush and rock salt, and it leaves these terrible white streaks all over the dark tile. You have to use a special chemical neutralizer just to get it up, you can't just mop it with regular soap or it just smears everywhere and looks worse than when you started. \n\nAnyway, I was dealing with that every single night. And during that whole stretch, maybe three, four weeks even, my mood was just... quiet. They were just calmer weeks, you know? I wasn't waking up feeling like I had that electricity in my blood, I wasn't yelling at anybody, and I definitely wasn't feeling deeply depressed or dragging my feet either. I was just regular. Just doing my job, buffing the floors, minding my business. \n\nBut the thing is, Dr. Smith, even during that time, for well over two weeks straight of just feeling completely level and normal in my energy... I still heard him. I still heard the man in the vents. Every night, clear as a bell over the sound of the floor buffer, telling me I ruined it all. And the signals didn't stop either. I'd be feeling perfectly fine, not high or low at all, but I’d see the night watchman adjust his belt, or leave his coffee cup exactly two inches from the edge of the security desk, and I knew—I just completely believed—that they were signaling about me in the building. It was all still happening. So, yeah, even without the mood swings, even when I'm just having a calm month, those things... the voices and the signals... they don't take a break.",
